{"id":"CVE-2004-1338","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-01-06T05:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T00:46:12.320Z","description":"The triggers in Oracle 9i and 10g allow local users to gain privileges by using a sequence of partially privileged actions: using CCBKAPPLROWTRIG or EXEC_CBK_FN_DML to add arbitrary functions to the SDO_CMT_DBK_FN_TABLE and SDO_CMT_CBK_DML_TABLE, then performing a DELETE on the SDO_TXN_IDX_INSERTS table, which causes the SDO_CMT_CBK_TRIG trigger to execute the user-supplied functions.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=110382230614420&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20041223 Oracle Trigger Abuse (#NISR2122004I)"},{"url":"http://www.ngssoftware.com/advisories/oracle23122004I.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/18655","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"oracle-triggers-gain-privileges(18655)"}],"vendors":["oracle-java"]}
